-- dispatch (project): result-only `where`, resolved across a module
-- boundary (§2.4, §4.2, §6.5, §7.2).
--
-- Nothing in `Main` mentions `a`; the two annotations are what pick the
-- function, one call apart from the dispatch that uses it. For that to
-- work the constraint has to survive the whole round trip — `decodeInto`'s
-- scheme is written to `Decoder`'s interface by `Schemes.Writer`, read back
-- by `Schemes.instantiate` here, and the canonical evidence order (§7.2)
-- has to be computed identically on both sides, from the scheme record
-- alone. A quantifier that occurs only in the RESULT is the case where
-- "walk the written body" could most easily have found a different order
-- in the callee than in the caller; it does not.
--
-- `top fromList` is this module's own type and `ext String fromList` is
-- core's, so one imported declaration answers two different functions and
-- the golden is what says which went where.
import Decoder
import String


pub type Tag
    = Tag String


pub fromList : List Char -> Tag
fromList chars =
    Tag (String.fromList chars)


pub asTag : Tag
asTag =
    Decoder.decodeInto "tag"


pub asString : String
asString =
    Decoder.decodeInto "str"
